        if (isBlank(request.getCity()))      missing.add("city");
        if (isBlank(request.getTelephone())) missing.add("telephone");
        if (!missing.isEmpty()) throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing);
        String e164 = OwnerTelephone.normalize(request.getTelephone());
        if (e164 == null) throw new InvalidTelephoneException("Telephone is not a valid E.164 number: " + request.getTelephone());
        request.setTelephone(e164);
        String email = OwnerEmail.normalize(request.getEmail());
        if (email != null && !OwnerEmail.isValid(email)) throw new InvalidEmailException("Email is not a valid address: " + request.getEmail());
        if (email != null && OwnerEmail.isDisposableDomain(email)) throw new InvalidEmailException("Email domain is a disposable-domain blocklist entry: " + request.getEmail());
        request.setEmail(email);
        validated.set(request);
    }
    private static boolean isBlank(String value) { return value == null || value.isBlank(); }
}
```
Note: binds `@RequestBody` **without** `@Valid` so missing-field checks produce the custom `errors` shape. This is the only step that binds the body; later steps read it via `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`.

### ValidateRegistrationDate.java
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) throws FutureRegistrationDateException {
    LocalDate supplied = request.getRegistrationDate();
    if (supplied != null && supplied.isAfter(LocalDate.now()))
        throw new FutureRegistrationDateException("registrationDate is later than the server date: " + supplied);
}
```

### ValidatePostcode.java
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request) throws InvalidPostcodeException {
    String postcode = request.getPostcode();
    if (!OwnerPostcode.isValid(postcode, request.getCity()))
        throw new InvalidPostcodeException("Postcode is not valid for city '" + request.getCity() + "': " + postcode);
}
```

### ResolveHousehold.java
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<Household.Id> householdIdOut) {
    householdIdOut.set(Household.idFor(request));
}
```

### ValidateUniqueIdentity.java (409 gate)
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, @Val Household.Id householdId,
        OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws DuplicateIdentityException {
    if (householdId == null || !householdId.isPresent()) return;          // no postcode => no household
    if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) return;         // declared member bypasses
    if (Household.hasMember(householdId.value(), null, ownerRepository))
        throw new DuplicateIdentityException("Household " + householdId.value() + " already has an owner (same last name and postcode)");
}
```

### ValidateCityCapacity.java (409, ≥50 per city)
```java
private static final int CITY_CAPACITY = 50;
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws CityAtCapacityException {
    String city = request.getCity();
    int count = 0;
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll())
        if (city.equalsIgnoreCase(existing.getCity())) count++;
    if (count >= CITY_CAPACITY) throw new CityAtCapacityException("City " + city + " already contains " + CITY_CAPACITY + " or more owners");
}
```

### ValidateDailyOwnerLimit.java (429, ≥100 per business day)
```java
private static final int DAILY_LIMIT = 100;
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws DailyOwnerLimitException {
    LocalDate businessDay = BusinessDay.effectiveRegistrationDate(request.getRegistrationDate());
    int count = 0;
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll())
        if (businessDay.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate())) count++;
    if (count >= DAILY_LIMIT) throw new DailyOwnerLimitException(DAILY_LIMIT + " or more owners have already been created on this business day");
}
```

### BuildOwner.java (maps DTO → entity, derives customerCode / householdId / counts)
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, @Val Household.Id householdId,
        OwnerMapper ownerMapper, OwnerRepository ownerRepository, Out<Owner> built) {
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(request);
    owner.setRegistrationDate(BusinessDay.effectiveRegistrationDate(owner.getRegistrationDate()));
    owner.setCustomerCode(deduplicate(customerCode(owner), ownerRepository));
    owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner.getFirstName(), owner.getLastName(), ownerRepository));
    if (householdId != null && householdId.isPresent()) owner.setHouseholdId(householdId.value());
    owner.setHouseholdSize(Household.size(owner.getHouseholdId(), ownerRepository) + 1);
    built.set(owner);
}
```
(Plus private helpers: `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` from region + SHA-256 of normalized telephone+lastName; `deduplicate` appends `-n`; `hash8`; `countNamesakes`.)

### SaveOwner.java
```java
public class SaveOwner {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        ownerRepository.save(owner);
    }
}
```

### AuditOwnerCreated.java
```java
private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT");
public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
    AUDIT.info("Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}",
        owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),
        owner.getMembershipLevel(), owner.getMembershipNumber());
}
```

### FlagBulkSignup.java (response-only flag, >80 created today)
```java
private static final int BULK_THRESHOLD = 80;
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    LocalDate today = BusinessDay.effectiveRegistrationDate(null);
    int count = 0;
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll())
        if (today.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate())) count++;
    owner.setBulkSignupWarning(count > BULK_THRESHOLD);
}
```

### FlagPossibleDuplicate.java (response-only soft match)
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    Integer match = PossibleDuplicate.matchOf(owner, ownerRepository);
    owner.setPossibleDuplicate(match != null);
    owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(match);
}
```

### RespondWithOwnerCreated.java (201 Created + Location)
```java
public class RespondWithOwnerCreated {
    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper,
            ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
        OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
        response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create(dto.getSelfLink())).body(dto));
    }
}
```

Supporting shared class **Household.java** (same dir): defines the `record Id(String value)` (with `ABSENT` and `isPresent()`), `idFor(OwnerFieldsDto)` (SHA-256 of `normalizedLastName|postcode`, first 12 upper hex), `hasMember(...)`, `size(...)` — all scanning only `ActiveOwners.list(...)` (ignores soft-deleted). Other helpers referenced: `OwnerAddress`, `OwnerTelephone`, `OwnerEmail`, `OwnerPostcode`, `BusinessDay`, `PossibleDuplicate`, `OwnerIdentity`, `ActiveOwners` (all in the same `function/owner/` package).

For contrast, the update path uses `ValidateOwner.java` (binds `@Valid @RequestBody`, email normalization) → `LoadOwner` (`@PathVariable(name="ownerId")`) → `ApplyOwner` → `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`.

---

## 3. Owner entity + DTOs

### Owner entity
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

JPA `@Entity @Table(name="owners")` extending `Person` (which supplies `firstName`/`lastName`). Persisted columns: `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, `city`, `telephone` (`@Pattern ^\+[0-9]{8,15}$` E.164), `email`, `title`, `registrationDate`, `birthDate`, `customerCode`, `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, `postcode`, `deleted` (soft-delete), plus `Set<Pet> pets`. `@Transient` (non-persisted) fields: `householdSize`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`. Many derived `@Transient` getters: `displayName`, `initials`, `salutation`, `telephoneDisplay`, `fiscalYear`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`, `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `timezone`, `contactPreference`, `ageBand`. Static region logic: `regionFor(postcode, city)`, `regionForCity`, `regionForPostcode` with `CITY_REGION`/`REGION_RANGE`/`REGION_TIMEZONE` maps. No `from()` factory method — construction is via the MapStruct mapper.

### DTOs — generated, not hand-written
`OwnerFieldsDto` and `OwnerDto` **do not exist as source files**. They are generated at build time by the **openapi-generator-maven-plugin** from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java`, package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`, with `modelNameSuffix=Dto`.

`OwnerFields` schema (`openapi.yml` lines ~1991-2110) → generates `OwnerFieldsDto` fields: `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, `city`, `telephone`, `email`, `title`, `postcode`, `registrationDate` (date), `birthDate` (date), `sharesHousehold` (boolean, **writeOnly**). Required: firstName, lastName, city, telephone.

`OwnerDto` = `allOf [OwnerFields + ...]` adding read-only derived fields (`id`, `pets`, `identityKey`, `selfLink`, `fiscalYear`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipPoints`, `membershipLevel`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `ageBand`, etc.).

### Mapper
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — MapStruct `@Mapper`. `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (ignores id/pets) builds the entity; `toOwnerDto(Owner)` adds `identityKey` (via `OwnerIdentity.of`) and `selfLink` (`"/api/owners/" + id`, null until persisted). `RespondWithOwnerCreated` sources its `Location` from `dto.getSelfLink()`.

---

## 4. Tests for creating owners

Test framework: **JUnit 5 (Jupiter)** + **Spring Boot Test** with **MockMvc** (`@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser`). Jackson via the `tools.jackson` (Jackson 3) `ObjectMapper`. OfficeFloor's `woof_test` dependency is on the test classpath. Endpoints are invoked through `MockMvc.perform(post("/api/owners")...)` / `get("/api/owners/{id}")` — black-box over HTTP, not by calling functions directly.

### AcceptanceTest.java
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`
```java
/** idempotency: a create that repeats with an already-seen 'Idempotency-Key' returns the
 * originally created owner with 200, instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise 409). */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {
    @Test
    void coreIdempotentRepeat() throws Exception {
        ObjectNode o = structuredOwner();
        String key = "idem-" + seq();
        int id1 = extractId(createOwnerWithKey(o, key).andExpect(status().is2xxSuccessful()));
        int id2 = extractId(createOwnerWithKey(o, key).andExpect(status().isOk()));
        assertEquals(id1, id2);
    }
}
```
This asserts: first POST with an `Idempotency-Key` → 2xx (201); second POST, same key + same body → **200 OK** with the **same owner id** (not a new owner, not a 409). Nothing in the application implements this yet.

### AcceptanceBase.java
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` (full source read; 322 lines). Relevant helpers:
- `createOwner(body)` → `post("/api/owners")` JSON.
- `createOwnerWithKey(body, key)` → same POST **plus `.header("Idempotency-Key", key)`**.
- `createOwnerOk`, `getOwner`, `fetchOwner`, `deleteOwner`, `extractId` (reads `id` from body, else parses `Location` header).
- Payload builders: `ownerNode()` (fully-unique valid owner), `withPostcode`, `structuredOwner()` (addressLine1 + postcode 2000), `knownOwner(city)`.
- Unique generators keyed off an `AtomicInteger SEQ` (`uniqueLastName`, `uniqueFirstName`, `uniqueTelephone` = `04XXXXXXXX`, etc.).
- Pinned reference tables (`CITY_REGION`, `REGION_TIMEZONE`, `REGION_POSTCODES`, `HOLIDAYS`) and algorithm replicas (`sha256hex`, `shaHex`, `luhn`, `toBusinessDay`).

These two are the only test files in the repo (`src/test/java/.../acceptance/`).

---

## 5. Idempotency grep results (whole repo)
`grep -rli "idempoten"` matched exactly three files:
1. `src/test/java/.../acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — the `coreIdempotentRepeat` test + class Javadoc.
2. `src/test/java/.../acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — `createOwnerWithKey` helper and its Javadoc ("the idempotent-create rule"), sends header `Idempotency-Key`.
3. `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/OwnerTelephone.java` — line 25, unrelated ("The function is idempotent: an already-E.164 …").

No match in `openapi.yml`, no YAML pipeline step, no function reads an `Idempotency-Key` header, no persistence/store for idempotency keys. Server-side idempotency is unimplemented.

---

## 6. OwnerRepository
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java` — plain interface (not a Spring Data repo directly; implementations under `repository/jdbc`, `repository/jpa`, `repository/springdatajpa`). Methods:
- `Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName)`
- `Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable)`
- `Owner findById(int id)`
- `void save(Owner owner)`
- `Collection<Owner> findAll()`
- `Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable pageable)`
- `void delete(Owner owner)`

(All `throws DataAccessException`. Note: no query for idempotency keys — an idempotency implementation would need its own store or a new repository/table.)

