## 7. Build & test

**Maven** (wrapper `./mvnw` present; `pom.xml` at repo root — not Gradle).
- Run app: `./mvnw spring-boot:run`
- Full build incl. generated sources + tests: `mvn clean install` (per readme.md line 218). DTO/API classes are generated at build time, so you must build through Maven (openapi-generator) before tests compile.
- Run just tests: `./mvnw test`.

OfficeFloor-relevant `pom.xml` entries:
- Property: `<officefloor.version>4.0.2</officefloor.version>` and a custom repo `officefloor-stage-repository` (`https://github.com/officefloor/maven/raw/repository/`).
- Main dependency: `net.officefloor.springboot:officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter:${officefloor.version}` (this is what wires the YAML pipelines into Spring Boot).
- Test dependency: `net.officefloor.web:woof_test:${officefloor.version}` (scope test).
- DTO generation: `org.openapitools:openapi-generator-maven-plugin:7.23.0`, `generatorName=spring`, `inputSpec=src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, `modelPackage=...rest.dto`, `apiPackage=...rest.api`, `modelNameSuffix=Dto`, output added to sources via `build-helper-maven-plugin` from `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java`.
- Other relevant deps: `spring-boot-starter-webmvc`, `-security`, `-validation`, `-jdbc`; `spring-boot-starter-test`, `-webmvc-test`, `-security-test`, `mockito-core`; Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson.core`); H2/HSQLDB/MySQL/Postgres drivers.

---

## 8. Directory layout

### `src/main/resources/officefloor/`
```
officefloor/
  escalation/          # one yml per exception -> HTTP status mapping
    java.lang.Exception.yml
    org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml
    org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.CityAtCapacityException.yml
    ...DailyOwnerLimitException.yml, DuplicateIdentityException.yml,
    FutureRegistrationDateException.yml, InvalidEmailException.yml,
    InvalidPostcodeException.yml, InvalidTelephoneException.yml,
    MissingOwnerFieldsException.yml, NotFoundException.yml,
    org.springframework.security.authorization.AuthorizationDeniedException.yml
    org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml
  rest/
    index.GET.yml
    api/
      owners.GET.yml
      owners.POST.yml                         <-- the create endpoint
      owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml
      owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml
      owners/{ownerId}.DELETE.yml
      owners/{ownerId}/pets.POST.yml
      owners/{ownerId}/pets/{petId}.GET.yml
      owners/{ownerId}/pets/{petId}.PUT.yml
      owners/{ownerId}/pets/{petId}/visits.POST.yml
      pets.GET.yml, pets/{petId}.{GET,PUT,DELETE}.yml
      pettypes.* , specialties.* , vets.* , visits.* , users.POST.yml
      v2/owners.GET.yml, v2/pets.GET.yml
```
Each escalation exception thrown by a function maps to an HTTP status via its `escalation/*.yml` (e.g. `DuplicateIdentityException` → 409, `DailyOwnerLimitException` → 429, the `Invalid*`/`Missing*` ones → 400).

### `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/`
```
ActiveOwners.java      ApplyOwner.java        AuditOwnerCreated.java
BuildOwner.java        BuildOwnersPet.java    BusinessDay.java
DeleteOwner.java       FlagBulkSignup.java    FlagPossibleDuplicate.java
Household.java         ListOwners.java        ListOwnersPage.java
LoadOwner.java         LoadOwnersPet.java     OwnerAddress.java
OwnerEmail.java        OwnerIdentity.java     OwnerPostcode.java
OwnerTelephone.java    PossibleDuplicate.java ResolveHousehold.java
RespondWithOwner.java  RespondWithOwnerCreated.java  RespondWithOwnerUpdated.java
SaveOwner.java         ValidateCityCapacity.java     ValidateDailyOwnerLimit.java
ValidateNewOwner.java  ValidateOwner.java     ValidatePostcode.java
ValidateRegistrationDate.java  ValidateUniqueIdentity.java
```
Sibling function packages: `rest/function/{common,pet,pettype,root,specialty,user,vet,visit}`. The model package `.../model/` holds `Owner.java`, `Person.java`, `Pet.java`, `BaseEntity.java`, etc.

### Notes for implementing idempotency (since the test expects it)
- A new pipeline step would go at the front of `owners.POST.yml` (before/around `validate`), read the header via a function `service(@RequestHeader(name="Idempotency-Key", required=false) String key, ...)` (Spring annotations are supported, as `LoadOwner` uses `@PathVariable`).
- On a hit it must short-circuit to a responder that returns **200** (not 201) with the previously-created `OwnerDto` — there is no existing mechanism to skip the rest of the pipeline or to store key→owner mappings, so a store (new table + repository, or in-memory) and a branch (`next`/flow) would be needed. No such infrastructure exists today.

